  <keyword>leapseconds</keyword>
  <short_description>Return leap second data available to the time module.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>L = leapseconds()</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>inputs</param_name>
      <param_description>No input arguments.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>output</param_name>
      <param_description>An array containing leap second data; currently empty when no leap-second table is embedded.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>Return leap second data available to the time module.</p>
    <p>The function is present for date and time API completeness. The current embedded timezone subset does not include leap second records.</p>
    <p>Array-valued inputs keep their data shape when the operation supports arrays. Scalar operands are expanded where the implementation defines scalar expansion.</p>
  </description>
